// What a new game's compile may cost (ticket 2009, ADR-0049, ADR-0120). CI's
// `compile-times` job runs `cargo xtask compile-times --budget` on this
// file (crates/xtask/src/compile_times.rs) and fails over it.
Budget(
    // The most a new `grid` game's rebuild after a one-line change in its
    // `main.rs` may take, as a ratio of a fixed reference build timed just
    // before it on the same runner (the median of three such pairs), by OS
    // (`std::env::consts::OS`). Seconds followed the runner's CPU: the same
    // code rebuilt in 0.87 to 1.33 s on Linux and 1.54 to 2.72 s on Windows,
    // while this ratio stayed within 1.069 to 1.171 on Linux and 1.136 to
    // 1.232 on Windows (calibration run 43775373036, 20 runs of each on
    // 9ac070d6). Each number is the highest measured plus 20 %, about twice
    // the ratio's spread. Checked over 20 more runs, calibration run
    // 43776381949 on 0f8c48fa: every run passed, at 1.066 to 1.174 on Linux
    // and 1.153 to 1.235 on Windows, while the seconds spread 0.76 to 1.35
    // and 1.39 to 2.84. `debug = true` in the template's `dev` profile
    // failed every run (calibration run 43776383981: 2.395 to 2.986). A
    // slower rebuild is found and fixed, not budgeted.
    rebuild_over_reference: {
        "linux": 1.40,
        "windows": 1.48,
    },
    // The most crates a new `blank` game's dependency tree may hold, the
    // engine's among them (`cargo metadata`, every platform's, with the
    // engine's Cargo.lock). A change that adds one raises this number in
    // the same PR, so each new dependency is a choice, and one that drops
    // some lowers it. 143: 146 less `quad-storage`, `quad-storage-sys`,
    // `nanoserde`, `nanoserde-derive` and `lazy_static`, gone with the
    // in-house web saves (ticket 3033), plus 2 for `getrandom` in
    // `reveal commit` (ticket 2816); set by ticket 2080. 149: plus 6 for
    // `shuyi new`'s prompts in a terminal (ticket 3423): `dialoguer`,
    // `console`, `shell-words`, `encode_unicode`, `unicode-width` and the
    // `windows-sys` `console` builds on, in the game's tools only.
    dependencies: 149,
)
